        "title": "fix(find): call stopChild in error handler for symmetric cleanup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nThe `child.on('error')` handler called `cleanup()` but not `stopChild?.()`, unlike the `child.on('close')` handler. Asymmetric cleanup on error paths.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nAdd `stopChild?.()` in the error handler to match the close handler pattern.\n\n## User Impact\nNo user-visible change. Symmetric cleanup on both handlers.\n\n## Evidence\n![proof](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zhangLei99586/openclaw/proof-screenshots/pr-98854-proof.png)\n- Source verified: `stopChild?.()` present in error handler",
